# First mode=menus session. No boss, no spec, no style on this axis -- the
# cell is just view (820x1180,touch) and save (carried). Nothing here is on a
# clock, so this starts short: list the front page, look, then decide the
# next three lines rather than scripting the whole session up front.
open
targets
ui
shot front

# The reset hitbox at 408,1084 300x40 matches #266 exactly (invisible while
# down=0, under the 44px floor) -- not new, moving on rather than re-filing.
tap raid
targets
ui
shot raidsetup

tap open:difficulty
targets
shot difficulty-open

# The 1F512 lock glyph next to "Heroic" drew as a missing-glyph box, not a
# padlock -- this machine has no emoji font installed (fc-list confirms),
# so this may be a test-environment artifact rather than something a real
# phone or desktop browser would show. Noted for direction.md, not filed.
#
# Picking the value that is already selected (Normal, while Normal) left the
# dropdown open on purpose -- src/main.ts's updateRaidSetup only closes it
# `if (moved(before, next))`, with a comment explaining why a no-op press
# should not read as having been taken. Not a bug; dismissing properly below.
tap dismiss
targets
shot difficulty-closed

tap next
targets
ui
shot classpick

tap compose
targets
ui
shot compose

# "tap anyone to change what they play" -- try it on a party member, not the
# AUTO/REROLL buttons, since nothing has poked at an individual slot before.
tap slot:1
targets
ui
shot slot-tapped

tap back
targets
shot backtoroster

tap back
targets
shot backfromclass

tap back
targets
shot backtohome

# Settings and the record, from the front page -- neither has been looked at
# by any prior session. (The three `back`s above landed on `raid`, not
# `home`: the composition screen's own back doubles as CANCEL while a spec
# picker is open, per src/render/composition.ts -- one more press than
# expected, and my script's math, not a bug. `open` sidesteps it.)
open
tap settings
targets
ui
shot settings

open
tap record
targets
ui
shot record
